{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JWgQNbyBDkpZxmTYzDu5DP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via an AI orchestrator, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Implementation state** (from source_code, which overrides prose):\n- `pkg/testutils/` — exists: `difftest.go` (R1-R5), `runner.go`\n- `pkg/format/` — partially exists: `color.go` (R2), `size.go` (R3); **R1 (column alignment) is missing**\n- `pkg/sys/` — partially exists: `stat.go` + platform files (R2); terminal size, signal handling, process group, process priority are missing\n- `cmd/` — no utilities on working branch\n\n**Current release**: 00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure), use cases: uc001-magefiles, uc002-format, uc003-sys, uc004-testutils.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 has four use cases. From source code: testutils (uc004) appears complete (R1-R5 implemented), format (uc002) is missing R1 (column alignment), sys (uc003) is missing terminal/signal/process capabilities, and magefiles (uc001) targets only `cmd/version` per DD7.\n\nThe highest-value next task is **prd003-format R1 (column alignment)** because:\n1. It completes the format package for uc002-format\n2. It's needed downstream by `cmd/ls` and `cmd/du` (tabular output)\n3. The package exists with clear conventions to follow (color.go, size.go)\n4. It fits the 150–250 line target\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd003-format R1 -- Column alignment for tabular output\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (full PRD for format package -- R1 covers column alignment)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (use case for format package in release 00.0)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test suite covering release 00.0 acceptance criteria)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (existing R2 implementation -- follow copyright header, package doc, and requirement tracing conventions)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (existing R3 implementation -- follow HumanSizeOpts pattern for configuration structs)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/align.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment implementation for tabular output (ls -l style)\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement column alignment per prd003-format R1: compute column widths from a set of rows and pad each cell to produce aligned tabular output matching GNU ls -l formatting\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Support both left-aligned (text) and right-aligned (numeric) columns per prd003-format R1 sub-requirements\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Follow existing pkg/format conventions: copyright header (2026 Petar Djukic, MIT SPDX), package doc comment, prd003-format R1 requirement tracing comments on all exported symbols\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Use only Go standard library (fmt, strings); no external dependencies per project technology choices\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"File named align.go, derived from the alignment feature described in ARCHITECTURE.yaml pkg/format component\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the options-struct pattern established by HumanSizeOpts in size.go if configuration is needed\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All exported functions include prd003-format R1.x requirement tracing comments matching the // (prd003-format R1.x) pattern used in color.go and size.go\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/format/align.go exists and compiles with go build ./pkg/format/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Exported alignment functions produce correctly padded tabular output for mixed-width input\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"golangci-lint passes on pkg/format/ with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Every prd003-format R1 sub-requirement is implemented and traced with a source comment\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":44198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7842,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a400a33-d2d4-46bd-b5d9-d41ed462b733","uuid":"19eec509-f32b-4004-9ad3-000000000001"}
